Backport of https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/199691 (upstream
commits a027f67b3ef76e04e7150730e86101791d385274 and
f811c7054289b5402f7dc3f234a31c8f6c65f6ab) fixing
https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/199224:

After 782bf6aff6ba ("x86: fix musttail sibcall miscompilation", present
in release/22.x as 0f73e77781a2), a musttail call with matching calling
convention was always treated as a sibling call, which skips the stores
of outgoing stack arguments. Any argument passed on the stack was
silently dropped, e.g. the 7th argument of a musttail tailcc call.

This miscompiles WebKit/Skia raster pipelines (SkRasterPipeline_opts.h
and skcms use [[clang::musttail]] for every pipeline stage) and
JavaScriptCore, producing wrong rendering results or crashes.

Only treat musttail as a sibling call when every argument is in a
register; otherwise full tail-call lowering must run to populate the
outgoing stack slots. The upstream fix was restructured against a newer
LowerCall; this is the equivalent change for the release/22.x code
layout, with the all_of-based condition spelled as a plain loop.
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/X86/X86ISelLoweringCall.cpp
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/X86/X86ISelLoweringCall.cpp
@@ -2143,6 +2143,16 @@
                                                   IsCalleePopSRet);
 
-    if (!IsMustTail) {
+    if (IsMustTail) {
+      // Treat musttail as a sibcall only when every argument is in registers;
+      // otherwise full tail-call lowering must run to populate the outgoing
+      // stack slots (llvm/llvm-project#199224).
+      for (const CCValAssign &VA : ArgLocs) {
+        if (!VA.isRegLoc()) {
+          IsSibcall = false;
+          break;
+        }
+      }
+    } else {
       isTailCall = IsSibcall;
       IsSibcall = IsSibcall && !ShouldGuaranteeTCO;
     }
